    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d389-a1">

                <pb facs="1345" n="1310" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v09Ed2/pg1310"/>


                <head><hi rendition="#bold">Alert Memorandum for the National Security Council
                        Prepared in the Central Intelligence Agency</hi><anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d389-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1980-07-11">July 11, 1980</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Syria</item>
                </list>
                <p>Although not imminent, Syrian President Assad’s assassination or overthrow is
                    significantly more likely today than it was before the 26 June assassination
                    attempt. I believe that US policymakers need to focus sooner rather than later
                    on the potential adverse regional consequences of Assad’s removal from the
                    scene. The attached Alert Memorandum outlines briefly some of these regional
                    implications. [<hi rendition="#italic">handling restriction not
                        declassified</hi>]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#bold">Frank C. Carlucci</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d389-f1" n="4" type="source" xml:id="d389-f1-content">
                <p>Secret; [<hi rendition="#italic">handling restriction not declassified</hi>].
                    Brzezinski added a handwritten notation to Hunter, Sick, Odom, and Ermarth,
                    dated July 15, in the upper right-hand corner of the memorandum: “Pl[ea]se get
                    together and discuss—give me your recom[mendation]s. ZB.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
